  "gridRows": 3,
  "idPrefix": "doodad.toxic-ground",
  "note": "A toxic world's ground, drawn in place of the default art by urban.mapping.json's paletteGroundRender for SurfacePalette.TOXIC: STONE is toxic-ground.crust (corroded, chemically stained olive regolith), SAND is toxic-ground.sulphur (crusted sulphur flats) and WATER is toxic-ground.sludge (standing acid sludge, impassable because it is WATER). Measured: 448x168, RGB with no alpha, a fused plate cut on its 8x3 grid of 56 px cells, one row per family of eight variants.\n\nEvery cell takes its picture from a tileable material under atlas-material-source/toxic-*-variants, so the plate is only a contact sheet of them: regenerate a family by re-running normalize_ground_variants.py on the masters in toxic-ground/ (crust --scale 3; sulphur --scale 3 --band 13; sludge --scale 4 --band 13, cut from 480 px crops, since its smooth liquid fails the seam check with the blend wrap), then rebuild this plate. Its own sheet rather than cells on Floors_Tiles, so other palettes' ground can be added without re-packing the shared floors atlas.",
  "sheet": "art-source/tilesets/toxic-ground.raw.png",
  "sheetName": "toxic-ground"
}